# {{PLUGIN_NAME}}

Processor and editor sources live in `src/`. Format entry points, when present,
live in `src/entry/`. C++ tests live in `tests/`.

Install the [Pulp CLI](https://www.generouscorp.com/pulp/), then run:

```sh
pulp build
pulp test
```

`pulp.toml` selects the SDK version. To install an exact pin ahead of the build,
run `pulp sdk install --version <version>`. A project using `latest` tracks the
newest installed SDK. Use `pulp project pin <version>` to lock the version.

For a private SDK build, run `pulp sdk install --local --print-path` from its
Pulp checkout. Use the returned prefix with CMake in a fresh build directory:

```sh
cmake -S . -B build -DPulp_DIR=/path/to/sdk/lib/cmake/Pulp
```

Keep this path in your local CMake cache or shell environment. Projects created
with `--ui vellum` need a Pulp SDK built with `PULP_ENABLE_PULP_VELLUM=ON` and a
matching Vellum CMake package. Set `Vellum_DIR` for local builds and provision
both packages on the CI runner.
